---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = '2026-06-05';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy – Ynvesters"
  description="Privacy policy for Ynvesters — how we handle data, cookies, and third-party advertising."
>
  <div style="max-width: var(--max-width); margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem; line-height:1.8;">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--color-text-muted); font-size:0.9rem; margin-bottom:2rem;">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>1. Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Ynvesters ("we", "us", "our") operates ynvesters.com (the "Site"). This Privacy Policy describes
      what information is collected when you use the Site, how it is used, and your rights regarding that information.
      By using the Site, you agree to the practices described in this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We do not directly collect or store personal information from visitors. The following third-party services
    may collect data automatically when you visit the Site:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> May log IP addresses for security, DDoS protection, and performance analytics.</li>
      <li><strong>Google AdSense:</strong> Uses cookies and similar tracking technologies to serve advertisements relevant to you.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics (if enabled):</strong> Collects anonymized usage statistics such as page views, session duration, and browser type.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small text files placed on your device. This Site uses third-party cookies from:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google AdSense / DoubleClick:</strong> Used for ad targeting and measurement.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Used for aggregated traffic analysis.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can control cookie preferences through your browser settings. Disabling cookies may affect the
      functionality of some features. To opt out of personalized Google advertising, visit
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.
      You can also use the <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NAI opt-out tool</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Google AdSense</h2>
    <p>
      We participate in Google AdSense, an advertising service provided by Google LLC. Google uses cookies,
      including the DoubleClick cookie, to serve ads based on your prior visits to this Site or other websites.
      Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to our
      site and/or other sites on the Internet.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may review Google's Privacy Policy at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>
      and Google's Terms and Conditions at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/terms</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. California Privacy Rights (CCPA)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a California resident, you have the right to know what personal data is collected about you,
      to request deletion of your personal data, and to opt out of the sale of personal data.
      Because we do not directly collect personal data, these rights are primarily exercised through the
      third-party services listed above. For requests, please contact us via our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. European Visitors (GDPR)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are visiting from the European Economic Area (EEA), you have rights under the General Data
      Protection Regulation (GDPR), including the right to access, rectify, or erase personal data held
      about you. Google's consent management platform handles consent for EU/EEA visitors where applicable.
      For further inquiries, contact us via our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>
      Our articles link to external websites. We are not responsible for the content or privacy practices
      of those sites. We encourage you to review the privacy policy of every site you visit.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This Site is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information
      from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us
      and we will take steps to delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be reflected by the "Last updated"
      date at the top of this page. Continued use of the Site after any changes constitutes acceptance of
      the new policy.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy-related questions or requests, please use our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
